{"units": [{"id": "aner-quote11", "translation": "from men and from women's companies."}, {"id": "aner-quote12", "translation": "For a woman deprives each man of his life."}, {"id": "aner-quote13", "translation": "And the beds of men are filled with tears through longing."}, {"id": "aner-quote14", "translation": "Persian women longing to see the recent union of their husbands."}, {"id": "aner-quote15", "translation": "of a man (Agamemnon) who had sent word from Troy to me (Clytemnestra)."}, {"id": "aner-quote16", "translation": "to a man."}, {"id": "aner-quote17", "translation": "her own husband."}, {"id": "aner-quote18", "translation": "the bed of a husband."}, {"id": "aner-quote19", "translation": "from a dear wife to a dear husband."}, {"id": "aner-quote20", "translation": "And she exchanged her husband for Aegisthus."}, {"id": "aner-quote21", "translation": "to bury a husband."}, {"id": "aner-quote22", "translation": "of a man."}, {"id": "aner-quote23", "translation": "For what is a woman who deprives her husband of life?"}, {"id": "aner-quote24", "translation": "She strikes him, having bound her husband in a cunning robe."}, {"id": "aner-quote25", "translation": "For a marriage bed is fated for a man and a woman."}, {"id": "aner-quote26", "translation": "the beds of men."}, {"id": "aner-word1", "translation": "man (genitive singular), man (dative singular), man (accusative singular), men (nominative plural), men (genitive plural), men (accusative plural)"}, {"id": "aner-word2", "translation": "a mortal man"}, {"id": "aner-word3", "translation": "of men"}, {"id": "aner-word4", "translation": "man (corrupt form)"}, {"id": "aner-word5", "translation": "human being"}, {"id": "aner-word6", "translation": "another"}, {"id": "aneres-orth1", "translation": "manly"}, {"id": "aneres-def1", "translation": "manly"}, {"id": "aneres-note1", "translation": "which Hesychius explains by ἀνδρώδης [manly]"}, {"id": "aneres-note2", "translation": "A word not known from elsewhere. Concerning ἀνὴρ εις [man ...] in Sophocles Trach. 460, absurdly taken by the scholiast for ἀνήρεις [manly ones], I have spoken in my note on the scholia to Sophocles vol. 2 p. 71."}, {"id": "aneres-word1", "translation": "manly"}, {"id": "aneres-word2", "translation": "man ..."}, {"id": "aneres-word3", "translation": "manly ones"}, {"id": "anerithmos-orth1", "translation": "countless"}, {"id": "anerithmos-def1", "translation": "countless"}, {"id": "anerithmos-quote1", "translation": "and the countless laughter of the sea waves."}, {"id": "anerotos-orth1", "translation": "unplowed"}, {"id": "anerotos-def1", "translation": "unplowed"}, {"id": "anerotos-quote1", "translation": "go through unplowed fields."}, {"id": "anthaliskomai-orth1", "translation": "to be captured in turn"}, {"id": "anthaliskomai-def1", "translation": "to be captured in turn"}, {"id": "anthaliskomai-note1", "translation": "Thus Auratus for ἂν [if] (or α) θάνοιεν ἄν [they might die]."}, {"id": "anthaliskomai-quote1", "translation": "not those who have taken them might in turn be taken."}, {"id": "anthaliskomai-word1", "translation": "if"}, {"id": "anthaliskomai-word2", "translation": "they might die"}, {"id": "anthemizomai-orth1", "translation": "to gather flowers"}, {"id": "anthemizomai-def1", "translation": "to gather flowers"}, {"id": "anthemizomai-note1", "translation": "Improperly"}, {"id": "anthemizomai-note2", "translation": "i.e. I suffer the utmost torments."}, {"id": "anthemizomai-quote1", "translation": "and I gather flowers of lamentation."}, {"id": "anthemourgos-orth1", "translation": "working from flowers, like a bee"}, {"id": "anthemourgos-def1", "translation": "working from flowers, like a bee"}, {"id": "anthemourgos-quote1", "translation": "and the drop of the flower-worker, the all-shining honey."}, {"id": "anthemodes-orth1", "translation": "flowery"}, {"id": "anthemodes-def1", "translation": "flowery"}, {"id": "anthemodes-quote1", "translation": "of flowery spring."}, {"id": "antheo-orth1", "translation": "to bloom"}, {"id": "antheo-def1", "translation": "to bloom"}, {"id": "antheo-def2", "translation": "with dative, to abound, to overflow"}, {"id": "antheo-note1", "translation": "Improperly and in a bad sense"}, {"id": "antheo-note2", "translation": "as Sophocles Trach. 1089 said ἤνθηκεν [it has bloomed] of a disease."}, {"id": "antheo-quote1", "translation": "and for one who remains, suffering blooms."}, {"id": "antheo-quote2", "translation": "we see the Aegean sea blooming with corpses."}, {"id": "antheo-word1", "translation": "Trach. 1089 it has bloomed"}, {"id": "anthistamai-orth1", "translation": "to resist, to oppose"}, {"id": "anthistamai-def1", "translation": "to resist, to oppose"}, {"id": "anthistamai-note1", "translation": "[Pr. 354 ἀντέστη [he resisted] wrongly for ἀνέστη [he stood up]. See ἀνίστημι [to raise up].]"}, {"id": "anthistamai-quote1", "translation": "But since old fear of your mind resists."}, {"id": "anthistamai-word1", "translation": "he resisted"}, {"id": "anthistamai-word2", "translation": "he stood up"}, {"id": "anthistamai-word3", "translation": "to raise up"}, {"id": "anthonomeo-orth1", "translation": "to feed on flowers"}, {"id": "anthonomeo-def1", "translation": "to feed on flowers"}, {"id": "anthonomeo-quote1", "translation": "feeding on flowers of the ancestral cow."}, {"id": "anthonomos-orth1", "translation": "whose flowers are fed upon"}, {"id": "anthonomos-def1", "translation": "whose flowers are fed upon"}, {"id": "anthonomos-note1", "translation": "Which the scholiast explains by κατανομάς [pastures]."}, {"id": "anthonomos-quote1", "translation": "the flower-fed haunts of the mother."}, {"id": "anthonomos-word1", "translation": "pastures"}, {"id": "anthos-orth1", "translation": "flower"}, {"id": "anthos-def1", "translation": "flower"}, {"id": "anthos-def2", "translation": "Improperly, of blooming color"}, {"id": "anthos-def3", "translation": "the highest, the most excellent"}, {"id": "anthos-def4", "translation": "ornament"}, {"id": "anthos-note1", "translation": "Of the flower of youth"}, {"id": "anthos-quote1", "translation": "and woven flowers, children of the all-nourishing earth."}, {"id": "anthos-quote2", "translation": "meadow flowers."}, {"id": "anthos-quote3", "translation": "the flower of changing complexion."}, {"id": "anthos-quote4", "translation": "and let the unplucked flower of youth be."}, {"id": "anthos-quote5", "translation": "and the martial flower of Arabia."}, {"id": "anthos-quote6", "translation": "such a flower of the Persian land is gone, of men."}, {"id": "anthos-quote7", "translation": "and the flower of the Persians is gone, fallen."}, {"id": "anthos-quote8", "translation": "many men, the flower of the land."}, {"id": "anthos-quote9", "translation": "they were ravaging the flower of the Argives."}, {"id": "anthos-quote10", "translation": "the soul-biting flower of love."}, {"id": "anthos-quote11", "translation": "the choice flower of many possessions."}, {"id": "anthos-quote12", "translation": "for your flower, the light of all-crafting fire."}, {"id": "anthrakoo-orth1", "translation": "to turn into coals, to burn up"}, {"id": "anthrakoo-def1", "translation": "to turn into coals, to burn up"}, {"id": "anthrakoo-quote1", "translation": "burned to coals by the thunderbolt of Zeus."}, {"id": "anthropeios-orth1", "translation": "human"}, {"id": "anthropeios-def1", "translation": "human"}, {"id": "anthropeios-quote1", "translation": "respecting human blame."}, {"id": "an_2_see-orth1", "translation": "if"}, {"id": "an_2_see-quote1", "translation": "but human misfortunes might happen to mortals."}, {"id": "an_2_see-quote2", "translation": "know not to revere human things too much."}, {"id": "anthropomorphos-orth1", "translation": "having human form"}, {"id": "anthropomorphos-def1", "translation": "having human form"}]}